    <section id="privacy-notice" aria-labelledby="privacy-notice-heading" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h3 id="privacy-notice-heading" class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">A. Privacy Notice</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">The PIT Facility and Equipment Request System (PITFR) collects only the personal information needed to manage accounts and reservations. Depending on your account type and the request you make, this may include:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>your name, email address and contact number;</li>
            <li>your account type (student, faculty, staff or outsider), and your college, department, office or organization;</li>
            <li>reservation details: the activity, its purpose, schedule, venues, equipment and expected participants;</li>
            <li>supporting documents and the e-signature you upload with a request;</li>
            <li>an identification document submitted to verify your account;</li>
            <li>the decisions, remarks and notifications connected with your requests.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3"><strong class="text-slate-900">How it is collected:</strong> from what you enter when you register, submit or update a request, and from the actions that reviewers record on your request.</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-slate-900">How it is used and stored:</strong> it is stored in the PITFR system and used only for the purposes listed in section B. It is visible only to the people whose role requires it: you see your own requests, custodians see requests for the venues or equipment assigned to them, and the Supply Office reviews and decides on requests. The public calendar shows schedules only, never contact details.</p>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-slate-900">Identification documents:</strong> an uploaded ID is stored privately, can be opened only by authorized Supply Office staff, and is deleted once it has been reviewed. Only the ID type, the review result, the reviewer and the date are kept.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 p-3 text-emerald-900">Personal information in PITFR is handled in accordance with Republic Act No. 10173, the Data Privacy Act of 2012, and the applicable policies of Palompon Institute of Technology.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="purpose-of-data-collection" aria-labelledby="purpose-heading" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h3 id="purpose-heading" class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">B. Purpose of Data Collection</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">The information is used for:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">User account management and authentication:</strong> creating, verifying and securing your account and signing you in.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Reservation submission and processing:</strong> receiving your request and the documents that support it.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Venue and equipment scheduling:</strong> checking availability and preventing double bookings.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Reservation approval and coordination:</strong> routing the request to the custodians, coordinating offices and the Supply Office that review it.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Notifications and transaction records:</strong> sending you status updates and keeping a history of each request and the decisions made on it.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="data-protection" aria-labelledby="data-protection-heading" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h3 id="data-protection-heading" class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">C. Data Protection</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">PITFR applies appropriate organizational, physical and technical security measures to protect personal information against unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration or loss. These include password-protected accounts, access limited by each user's role and assignment, private storage for uploaded documents and IDs, records of who reviewed or acted on a request, and encrypted connections to the system.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Please upload only the information your request needs, and keep your password private.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="data-privacy-rights" aria-labelledby="privacy-rights-heading" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h3 id="privacy-rights-heading" class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">D. Data Privacy Rights</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">Under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173), and subject to the conditions and exceptions set by law, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">be informed</strong> that your personal information is being collected and processed;</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">access</strong> the personal information held about you;</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">object</strong> to processing, where the law allows;</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">rectify</strong> information that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">erasure or blocking</strong> of information, where the law allows;</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">data portability</strong>, to obtain a copy of your information in a usable format;</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">file a complaint</strong> with the National Privacy Commission;</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-900">damages</strong> for harm caused by unlawful processing.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">You can review and update much of your own information in your account settings.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="border-t border-slate-200 pt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">This page explains how PITFR handles and protects personal information. It does not replace the institution's official Data Privacy Policy or its obligations under RA 10173.</p>
</article>
